    "body": "The `lsp_fallback` field was deprecated in https://github.com/stevearc/conform.nvim/pull/456. `conform` [still supports](https://github.com/stevearc/conform.nvim/blob/238f542a118984a88124fc915d5b981680418707/lua/conform/init.lua#L444-L445) the `lsp_fallback` field for backwards-compatibility, but it seemed prudent for MiniMax to be using the newer field. `conform` has supported the new field since its v6.0.0 release in June 2024.",
    "closed_at": "2026-01-13T18:53:57Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR! It turns out this option was deprecated around 1.5 years ago! Didn't notice thanks to good backward compatibility. Another reason to use 'stevearc/conform.nvim' :)\r\n\r\nI've taken an opportunity and slightly reworked the whole setup: made keymaps more straightforward and setup `lsp_format` behavior globally.\r\n\r\nThis should now be fixed on latest `main`.",
            "created_at": "2026-01-13T18:59:33Z",
